# STIG RHEL-09-251020: firewalld firewalld-running
# STIG ID: V-257937 (MEDIUM)

META
    esp_id `r9-rhel-09-251020-firewalld-running-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `rocky9`
    criticality `high`

    title `STIG RHEL-09-251020: The RHEL 9 firewall must employ a deny-all, allow-by-exception policy for allowi`
    description `The RHEL 9 firewall must employ a deny-all, allow-by-exception policy for allowing connections to other systems.`
    author `example-security`
    tags `rhel9,stig,disa-stig,firewall`

    control_mapping `DISA-STIG:RHEL-09-251020,NIST-800-53:CM-6`
    control_objective `CM-6`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Rocky9:localhost:os-hardening`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Review and remediate per DISA STIG guidance for RHEL-09-251020.`

    component_id `comp-r9-os`

    impl_CM_6 `This control is validated by checking the required system configuration against the DISA STIG baseline for RHEL 9.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT fw_check
        zone `public`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE fw_state
        found boolean = true
        running boolean = true
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN firewalld_rule
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF fw_state
            OBJECT_REF fw_check
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
